	The mediant-sbc module recognizes the following options:
	(See above cisco-ios/cisco-cat section for descriptions.)

	user		Mandatory. Login name (SSH or telnet).
	pass		Mandatory. Login password.
	enable		Mandatory. The "enable" password: the CLI lands on
			the unprivileged "hostname> " prompt and the config
			is read from the privileged "hostname# " prompt.
			A wrong enable password is reported as such.
	transport	Optional. "ssh" (default), "telnet" or "auto".
			"auto" tries SSH first and falls back to telnet
			ONLY if no SSH service answers (connection refused,
			unreachable, timed out). It never falls back on an
			authentication, key-exchange or host-key failure:
			that would retry the password over a second channel
			(lockouts, alarms) and move a credential from an
			encrypted to a cleartext channel. A fallback is
			logged at info level so a downgrade is always
			visible.
	repository	Mandatory.
	keep		Mandatory.
	timeout		Optional, default 30 seconds (see the cisco-ios/
                        cisco-cat section).
	banner_timeout	Optional.
	prompt_settle_ms Optional (SSH). Milliseconds to wait for output
			to go idle before matching the prompt (default 150).
	fetch_timeout	Optional. The full configuration is long; raise
			this on slow links.
	changes_only	Optional.
	on_fetch_run	Optional.
	on_fetch_cat	Optional.
	timezone	Optional.
	filename_append_suffix Optional.
	show_cmd	Optional. Replaces "show running-config" (settings
			that differ from the firmware defaults - the form the
			device's own CLI-script export produces and a restore
			via "copy cli-script from ..." is designed for).
			"show running-config full" lists every parameter
			including defaults: better for auditing default
			changes across firmware upgrades, riskier to replay
			on a newer firmware. For both, add a second device
			entry with its own dev_id, e.g.
			  mediant-sbc SBC10      sbc10.example.com
			  mediant-sbc SBC10-full sbc10.example.com show_cmd="show running-config full"
			The CLI pauses with
			" --MORE--" after each screen. The pager settings are
			under "configure system" -> "cli-settings":
			default-window-height is persistent (part of the
			running configuration) and the per-session override
			window-height exists only inside that configuration
			mode. A backup tool must not modify the configuration
			nor enter configuration mode, so the pager is driven:
			a space is sent
			at every marker and the marker and its erase
			sequence are removed from the saved configuration.
	pager_cmd	Optional. A command to send before the show command
			to disable paging for the session, for a firmware
			that offers one. Its rejection ("Invalid command",
			"%", ...) aborts the fetch. Not needed on the
			observed Mediant 500Li.
	debug		Optional. Boolean. debug=on records to
			<repository>/<dev_id>.debug (mode 0600); over SSH the
			ssh client's debug trace comes first, then the raw
			session.

